{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011026-path-symbols-for-the-scelesti","id":1011026,"title":"Path Symbols For the Scelesti","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-02T05:39:08-08:00","id":1011026,"title":"Path Symbols For the Scelesti","content":"The Joining corrupts a Mage path symbols, inverting their form to suit the Nasnasi's broken self from consigning parth of their name to the Dur-Abzu.....<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Deluge:</b> Obrimos' who has undergone the Joining call upon symbols and beings of fallen glories, such as Satan the Fallen Angel whose pride reduced him to less than a bug or Jason who was crushed by the rotting ship that carried heroes and, of course, Atlantis itself. Some fallen Thaumaturge pilgrimage to Chernobyl, where men were unable to control the power that now damn the land for centuries to come or baptise themselves in the cold winds of the poles where they warm themselves to freeze themselves again and again. Others carry broken crosses, pray for despair, and invoke the faceless saints who said false truths to the holy that tortured them. Scelestus Theurgist gain power from objects that warps truth, such as dirty mirrors, rusted steel, and glitching computers, all turn light meaningless. </div> </div> </div>This thread is basically an excuse to discuss examples of Path Yantras for the Nasnasi, for resources or just for inspiration","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11724-backtoback","name":"backtoback","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T05:55:09-08:00","id":1011030,"title":"","content":"The Burning Iron Spiral: They are not Thyrsus anymore, not in anyway that matters.The sons of The Burning Iron Spiral eschew all balance and harmony. They create ritual magicks by destroying nature;It's imp\u00f3rtant that the destruction must be pointless and must serve a necessarily selfish purpose. They decorate the sanctuns with disgustingly crippled mutated animals,with excuse with garbage. Their greatest sanctuns are twisted palaces of metal that stood where once a ecossystem was incinerated. They inject drugs and medications or burn plastic and tires,everything that is manmade and notnatural can be used to power their evil spells<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T06:31:51-08:00","id":1011040,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I don't like it. Nasnasi Thyrsoi prize 'adaptation without integrity' it seems to me they're more magath, and Drugs that kills you even though it's the thing that allows you to live(I can imagine one Mystery Play based on chemotherapy) instead of Captain Planet villain. They value degradation and evolutionary dead ends over extinction at least, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11724-backtoback","name":"backtoback","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T07:05:37-08:00","id":1011061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>backtoback</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011026-path-symbols-for-the-scelesti?p=1011040#post1011040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I don't like it. Nasnasi Thyrsoi prize 'adaptation without integrity' it seems to me they're more magath, and Drugs that kills you even though it's the thing that allows you to live(I can imagine one Mystery Play based on chemotherapy) instead of Captain Planet villain. They value degradation and evolutionary dead ends over extinction at least, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I see it. Nasnasi of the Burning Iron Spiral are defined by a lack of purpose. Because everything in nature has a purpose, even death in destruction, it's all part of a circle of life that is ultimatelyy benevolent. The Nasnasi are the ones fighting the balance. They want to take resources without replenishing them,they want to create mutations that deviate from evolutionary path. They want to make the world like the abyss and the best way of doing that is making sure everything that was not supposed to happen,happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T14:53:53-08:00","id":1011232,"title":"","content":"The Abyssal Joining is a contradiction to the Supernal Path; an inversion of everything good; a reflection in a dark mirror. Abyssal Watchtowers are the accumulated antitheses of every Mage who has dabbled in antinomian magic and corrupted their spells for power.<br /> <br /> This is a problem, because it gives the impression that the Abyssal Path is just going to the stereotypical opposite. The tainted Thyrsus loves cities, so the wisdom goes, and all Scelesti revel in pain and misery without purpose.<br /> <br /> This is wrong.<br /> <br /> The reason the Abyssal Watchtower looks like it does is because it is a rejection; the Joining a fundamental revocation of one's old identity. A Path is more than just a set of magical tricks; it is a declaration of a Mage's perspective and understanding of the world. To change one's Path is a rejection of the very seat of one's soul; a shattering of the things which define you because, apparently, they don't.<br /> <br /> The Abyssal Path is the Mage rejecting something fundamental about themselves. It is the Obrimos proclaiming the universe is ultimately random and better off that way; the Thyrsus deciding that life is awful and worthy only of extinction; the Moros, that change is undesirable and the universe best kept static and repetitive.<br /> <br /> The Burning Iron Spiral is cancer; senseless murder; environmental degradation; the pointless futility of broken systems. It is not these things because a Mage joined to the Abyssal Path (necessarily) idealizes them, but because the Mage must accept that they no longer reject or even embrace some aspect of them. They reject the Truths of their Path for a Lie.<br /> <br /> That's my take, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T16:11:41-08:00","id":1011265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011026-path-symbols-for-the-scelesti?p=1011232#post1011232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Abyssal Joining is a contradiction to the Supernal Path; an inversion of everything good; a reflection in a dark mirror. Abyssal Watchtowers are the accumulated antitheses of every Mage who has dabbled in antinomian magic and corrupted their spells for power.<br /> <br /> This is a problem, because it gives the impression that the Abyssal Path is just going to the stereotypical opposite. The tainted Thyrsus loves cities, so the wisdom goes, and all Scelesti revel in pain and misery without purpose.<br /> <br /> This is wrong.<br /> <br /> The reason the Abyssal Watchtower looks like it does is because it is a rejection; the Joining a fundamental revocation of one's old identity. A Path is more than just a set of magical tricks; it is a declaration of a Mage's perspective and understanding of the world. To change one's Path is a rejection of the very seat of one's soul; a shattering of the things which define you because, apparently, they don't.<br /> <br /> The Abyssal Path is the Mage rejecting something fundamental about themselves. It is the Obrimos proclaiming the universe is ultimately random and better off that way; the Thyrsus deciding that life is awful and worthy only of extinction; the Moros, that change is undesirable and the universe best kept static and repetitive.<br /> <br /> The Burning Iron Spiral is cancer; senseless murder; environmental degradation; the pointless futility of broken systems. It is not these things because a Mage joined to the Abyssal Path (necessarily) idealizes them, but because the Mage must accept that they no longer reject or even embrace some aspect of them. They reject the Truths of their Path for a Lie.<br /> <br /> That's my take, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically speaking their created from 'the fears, rejected philosophies, and unutterable desires of those who wrote their names' so learning antinomian magic doesn't really create them in anyway IMO<br /> <br /> But yes I agree","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11724-backtoback","name":"backtoback","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T13:32:02-08:00","id":1011635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011026-path-symbols-for-the-scelesti?p=1011232#post1011232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Abyssal Joining is a contradiction to the Supernal Path; an inversion of everything good; a reflection in a dark mirror. Abyssal Watchtowers are the accumulated antitheses of every Mage who has dabbled in antinomian magic and corrupted their spells for power.<br /> <br /> This is a problem, because it gives the impression that the Abyssal Path is just going to the stereotypical opposite. The tainted Thyrsus loves cities, so the wisdom goes, and all Scelesti revel in pain and misery without purpose.<br /> <br /> This is wrong.<br /> <br /> The reason the Abyssal Watchtower looks like it does is because it is a rejection; the Joining a fundamental revocation of one's old identity. A Path is more than just a set of magical tricks; it is a declaration of a Mage's perspective and understanding of the world. To change one's Path is a rejection of the very seat of one's soul; a shattering of the things which define you because, apparently, they don't.<br /> <br /> The Abyssal Path is the Mage rejecting something fundamental about themselves. It is the Obrimos proclaiming the universe is ultimately random and better off that way; the Thyrsus deciding that life is awful and worthy only of extinction; the Moros, that change is undesirable and the universe best kept static and repetitive.<br /> <br /> The Burning Iron Spiral is cancer; senseless murder; environmental degradation; the pointless futility of broken systems. It is not these things because a Mage joined to the Abyssal Path (necessarily) idealizes them, but because the Mage must accept that they no longer reject or even embrace some aspect of them. They reject the Truths of their Path for a Lie.<br /> <br /> That's my take, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting.<br /> <br /> Here's something:<br /> <br /> <b>Ao Si, the Mound of Thorns</b>: An Acanthus who takes the Dark Path and dines with Balor is still, technically, a Witch. They spin Fate and weave through stories, making of the world around them a novel. The difference is, the Nasnas does what she does not because she's writing the story, but because the plot demands it of her. They don't abandon free will completely, of course; ultimately, the story also demands conflict, and choice is a source of it. But they do abandon the idea of it as relevant. Destiny, to the Scion of Twilight, is a force as immutable as gravity and even more vicious when human attempts to fight it fail. Anything important is ultimately preordained, and attempts to fight or even greet it prepared only lead to greater suffering. So the Nasnas becomes her own warden, an impersonal hand of the future who seeks only to ensure the karmic punishments are properly ironic. To that end, their Yantras revolve around inevitability and the caprice of the gods who actually decide the course of the world. They invoke the Midgard Serpent, slain in his hour of victory in Ragnarok, the Golden Apple of Eris that led to the fall of Troy over divine vanity, and yes, the impossible situation that C\u00fa Chulaind found himself in that prevented him from fulfilling his geasa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}